{title: Newness of Life}
{subtitle: Romans 6:3–4; Matthew 28:18–20; 3:13–17; Acts 8:35–39}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 87}
{time: 3/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | ×8

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Down to the Jordan the Son of God came walking
John held him in the [Cm]water as the [Abmaj7]river rolled a[Bb]long
As soon as Jesus [Cm]was baptized, he [Abmaj7]came up out of the [Eb]water
And be[Cm]hold, a voice from [Bb]heaven said
[Ab]This is my beloved Son, in [Bb]whom I am well [Eb]pleased
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
So [Ab]through baptism we were [Eb]buried with him into [Bb]death
[Ab]In order that, [Eb]just as Christ was raised from the [Bb]dead
By the [Cm]glory of the Father
We [Bb]too might walk in [Ab]newness of life
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
On the [Eb]desert road from Jeru[Ab]salem a chariot was [Eb]turning
Philip [Cm]told the good news a[Ab]bout Jesus as they [Bb]rode
Look, here is [Cm]water
What [Ab]is to keep me from being bap[Eb]tized
And he [Cm]went on his way re[Bb]joicing down the [Eb]road
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Cm]Go and make disciples of all [Ab]nations
Bap[Eb]tizing them in the name [Bb]of the Father
[Cm]And of the Son and of [Ab]the Holy Spirit
And [Eb]remember, I am [Bb]with you always
To the [Ab]very end of the [Eb]age
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Abmaj7]We too might walk in newness of [Eb]life
Newness of [Abmaj7]life
{end_of_verse}

